session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Cross-epic ownership correction (2026-09-07): this story's claim that it edits exactly `docs/README.md:130` and `:142` and that \"every other line belongs to the docs epic\" is contradicted by two concurrent stories: courageous-charcoaly-wrasse (overlap epic) edits the same line `:142` (one sentence carrying four `calibration/` links, including `overlap_batch_confidence.md`, which it deletes), and dendriform-amethyst-hoopoe (editor epic) edits `:79`. Rule for `:142`: this story repoints the surviving links to `evals/calibration/`; the overlap story removes its one link; whichever lands second re-applies its edit to the sentence as it then stands. Also `tests/unit/test_check_criteria_vocabulary.py`: this story edits `:168,212`, the editor story `:169`, the MCP derivation story `:324-326`, and the test-suite story deletes one test; all disjoint, rebase-trivial.","timestamp":1788814890231486752},{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Cite re-verification against origin/main 360d504f5ceb (2026-09-07). No description cite moved: the only cited file that changed since 2e81cb9767c1 is `.github/codeql/codeql-config.yml`, whose comment block was condensed from 10 lines to 5 (file now 9 lines). The cited construct at `:4,7` (the two comment lines naming `docs/experiments/**`) NO LONGER EXISTS on the tip: the file no longer mentions `docs/experiments` at all (line 2 now says \"hand-run experiments\" without a path). The cite is left as written per the no-invented-lines rule; on the tip the story's CodeQL edit reduces to adding `evals/**` under `paths-ignore:` (`:8-9`), with no `docs/experiments` string to repoint. Only the basis sentence changed (2e81cb9767c1 -> 360d504f5ceb).","timestamp":1788838524671938001},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Cite drift audit against current `main` (`b6e723ceb59`), 2026-10-26. The description's cites are pinned to `360d504f5ceb`; main has moved well past it and **most line-numbered cites no longer point at the cited construct**. A plan review on the description as written would score citation accuracy against these. Verified directly in a clean worktree at `b6e723ceb59`:\n\n| Description cite | Truth on `b6e723ceb59` |\n|---|---|\n| `.gitignore:20,124-127` | `:19` (`criterion_firings.jsonl`) and `:123` (`replay/cache/`), comment at `:122` |\n| `scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py:50` | `:45` — `Path(\"docs/experiments\")` |\n| `pyproject.toml:397-398` (sdist `include`) | `:391` |\n| `docs/README.md:130` and `:142` | `:129` and `:141` — the file is **141 lines**, so `:142` does not exist |\n| `tests/unit/test_criterion_effectiveness.py:19` | `:16` |\n| `tests/unit/test_e6_agreement.py:16` | `:5` |\n| `tests/unit/test_gate_eval_classifier.py:17` | `:3` |\n| `tests/unit/test_impact_model_versioning.py:46` | `:41` |\n\nStill accurate, re-verified: `pyproject.toml:363-367` (wheel `packages = [\"src/rebar\"]`), `scripts/check_dco_identity.py:30` (`\"docs/experiments/\",`), `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_A1.md:10` (\"a path under docs/experiments/\"), `tests/unit/test_derive_code_review_threshold.py:12`.\n\n**A substantive change, not just a line-number refresh — CodeQL.** The 2026-09-07 comment recorded that `codeql-config.yml` no longer names `docs/experiments` and concluded the edit \"reduces to adding `evals/**` under `paths-ignore:`\". On the tip that file is 9 lines and its entire ignore list is `docs/**`. So today the research tree is excluded **only because it lives under `docs/`**. Moving it to a top-level `evals/` removes it from that umbrella, and CodeQL would begin scanning the 65 research `.py` files unless `evals/**` is added in the same change. That makes the CodeQL edit load-bearing for this story rather than cosmetic, and worth its own acceptance criterion — the current ACs do not cover it.\n\nAC4 (\"`git diff -U0 -- docs/README.md` has exactly two hunks (lines 130 and 142)\") needs restating to `:129` and `:141`.\n\nRecorded now so the description can be refreshed in one pass before `review-plan` runs. This ticket is not yet reviewable: it `depends_on` `d279-4cf9-d1a6-4f7b`, which is still `in_progress`, so `review-plan` fast-fails with no LLM until that closes.","timestamp":1793078675354586307},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Second audit pass (2026-10-26, worktree at `b6e723ceb59` + the landing `d279` change). Two things beyond the line-number drift already recorded.\n\n**1. `d279` introduces a test that this story will break.**\n\n`d279` adds `tests/unit/evals/test_evals_corpus_root.py::test_no_hard_coded_roots`, whose assertion is literally:\n\n```python\nassert [line.split(\":\")[0] for line in hits] == [\"src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/corpus.py\"]\n```\n\nIt greps `src/rebar/llm/evals` for `docs/experiments` and requires `corpus.py` to be the **sole** remaining match (that is `d279`'s AC1). This story's Approach repoints `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/corpus.py:5` to the new path — at which point the grep returns an EMPTY list and that assertion fails. The two stories are individually correct and jointly red.\n\nResolution belongs to this story, since it is the one that moves the tree: when `corpus.py`'s docstring is repointed, `test_no_hard_coded_roots` must be updated in the same change — either to expect no matches at all, or repointed at `evals`. Add `tests/unit/evals/test_evals_corpus_root.py` to `file_impact` and name the update in the Approach.\n\n**2. `file_impact` is missing 6 files that the story's own grep AC will catch.**\n\nAC2 requires the repo-wide grep to print nothing outside frozen fixtures and historical notes. These currently match and are **not** in `file_impact`:\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/config_readers.py` — the `[llm.evals]` section comment `d279` adds names `docs/experiments`\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_evals_corpus_root.py` — see item 1 (new in `d279`)\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_cli_paths.py` — module docstring (new in `d279`)\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_corpus.py` — note `d279`'s AC asserts this file is *unchanged*; that holds only until this story moves the tree\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_interpreter_v2.py`\n- `.rebar/evals/plan-review-project-failure-disposition-contract.eval.yaml`\n\nAlso `.test_durations` matches, but it is generated and should be left alone — worth stating explicitly so the grep AC does not read as requiring an edit there.\n\n**Line-number corrections for the remaining test cites** (first match per file, on `b6e723ceb59`), in addition to those in the previous comment:\n\n| Description cite | Actual |\n|---|---|\n| `test_decomp_shape_criterion.py:183` | `:179` |\n| `test_necessity_criterion.py:103` | `:98` |\n| `test_project_failure_disposition_contract.py:242` | `:222` |\n| `test_transition_force_flag_24f7.py:163-170` | `:148,149` |\n| `test_check_criteria_vocabulary.py:168,212` | `:169,210` |\n| `tests/unit/gold_set_completion.py:12` | **no match at all** — the reference is gone; drop it from Scope and `file_impact` |\n\nRe-verified as accurate: `test_ac_process_gate_criterion.py:118`, `test_asserted_capability_criterion.py:115`, `test_t15_overlay_derisk_criterion.py:156`, `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py:25`, `tests/unit/test_check_dco_identity.py:6,110`, `tests/scripts/test_classify_gerrit_verify_change.py:57-58`.\n\nWhole-tree count for sizing: 54 files currently match outside `docs/experiments/`, `docs/calibration/`, `tests/fixtures/`, `CHANGELOG.md` and `docs/release-notes.md`. The `docs/adr/` (4), `docs/research/` (1) and `docs/archive/` (1) hits are historical records and are correctly excluded by AC2's \"historical notes\" carve-out — worth naming them in Scope as deliberately untouched so a reviewer does not read the grep as requiring them.","timestamp":1793083797337788655}],"created_at":1788805688653567584,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"04b040c1-3608-49b2-a91a-305d46c78b50","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"d279-4cf9-d1a6-4f7b"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n13 MB of research artefacts live under `docs/experiments/`; `docs/calibration/` holds 4 notes plus `plan_v5_rescore.py`. Living under `docs/` makes them docs-tooling link-check targets and is the ONLY reason CodeQL skips them. Packaging is non-shipping: wheel `packages = [\"src/rebar\"]` (`pyproject.toml:363-367`), sdist `include` (`:391`), no `MANIFEST.in`. `scripts/check_docs_index.py` link-checks `docs` recursively (`:103`), so after the move it stops seeing the tree. Cites verified on `aa37a738570`.\n\n## Approach\n`git mv docs/experiments evals && git mv docs/calibration evals/calibration` (history preserved), then repoint every live reference OUTSIDE the moved tree.\n\n**The moved tree's own contents are frozen as authored.** 61 files / 157 lines inside the two trees embed the literal old paths — harness scripts, run artefacts, eval-spec fixtures, notes. Those strings record what was actually executed, so rewriting them would falsify the research record, as for `docs/archive/`. `evals/` is excluded from the AC2 grep.\n\n**The worklist is the Testing grep plus the relative-link grep below, not a hand-kept list** — successive hand enumerations each missed live references, so AC2 and AC7 enforce the target instead.\n\n- **`rebar.toml`** `:51` (a `docs/calibration/completion_floor.md` comment), `:216` (comment) and `:220` (`[llm.evals] corpus_root`, which flips to `\"evals\"`).\n- **`.gitignore`** `:19`, `:122` (a comment naming `replay/corpus-*.manifest.json`) and `:123`.\n- **CodeQL — load-bearing.** `codeql-config.yml`'s whole ignore list is `docs/**` (`:8-9`), so the tree is excluded ONLY by living under `docs/`. A top-level `evals/` leaves that umbrella and CodeQL would scan the 65 research `.py` files, so `evals/**` must be added under `paths-ignore` HERE.\n- **Live docs under `docs/`**: `architecture.md:312`, `plan-review-gate.md:126,142,198,281,473,1537,1562,1804`, `remediation-implementation-plan.md:180,188,306`, `review-kernel.md:35`. `docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md:8` is GENERATED from `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_A1.md:10`; repoint the reviewer source and regenerate rather than editing the guide.\n- **A SECOND axis the grep cannot see: relative markdown links.** `docs/*.md` links in as `](experiments/...)`/`](calibration/...)` with no `docs/` prefix, so AC2 can print nothing while every link still points at vacated paths and `check_docs_index.py`'s link check breaks. Six lines: `README.md:129,141` (7 links), `architecture.md:310,312`, `llm-framework.md:80,81` — each becomes `](../evals/...)`. Find with `git grep -n '](experiments/\\|](calibration/' -- 'docs/*.md'`; AC7 enforces it.\n- **Source/packaged data**: `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_A1.md:10` (\"a path under `evals/` (formerly `docs/experiments/`)\"); `src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json` `_comment`s at `:4,92,112,158,189,197,205`; `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_advisory.py:164` and `det_operator_attested.py:11`; `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/corpus.py:5` and `legacy_v4_baseline.py:2-6`; `src/rebar/llm/config_readers.py` (the `[llm.evals]` comment); the six eval-spec comments plus `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/README.plan-review.md:67`; `scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py:45`, `scripts/check_dco_identity.py:30`, `scripts/calibrate_completion_floor.py:9`.\n- **Carry no such string** (verified, dropped from the worklist): `src/rebar/grounding/resolve.py`, `src/rebar/llm/structured.py`, `tests/unit/gold_set_completion.py`.\n- **Tests — 21 files, 34 hits in THREE categories, not one.** (a) REPOINT: the harness path loaders (`test_impact_model_versioning.py` has TWO, `:41` and `:146`; `test_transition_force_flag_24f7.py` has four hits, `:148,149,150,153`), plus `test_canonical.py:83` and `test_code_review_criteria_routing.py:140`, the latter asserting `superseded_by == \"docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration-code-v5.md\"` and moving in step with `criteria_routing.json:4,158`. (b) COUPLED REPOINT — a fixture that must move with its script's allowlist, or the test breaks: `scripts/check_dco_identity.py:30` `EXCLUDED_PREFIXES` with `test_check_dco_identity.py:110`, and `scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py:45` with `test_check_criteria_vocabulary.py:169,210`. (c) FREEZE — the old string is the point, so repointing it would break the test: `test_removed_cli_verbs_heldout.py:44` and `test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py:25` hold `_HISTORY_PREFIXES` that scan git HISTORY, where `docs/experiments/` paths still exist in old commits — ADD `evals/`, keep the old prefix; `tests/scripts/test_classify_gerrit_verify_change.py:57,58` are synthetic classifier INPUTS, not references to the tree. Those three files stay in-grep, so AC2 excludes them by name.\n- **Sequencing on `d279` (`disgusted-fretful-hare`, closed).** It added `tests/unit/evals/test_evals_corpus_root.py::test_no_hard_coded_roots`, which asserts `corpus.py` is the SOLE `docs/experiments` match under `src/rebar/llm/evals` (its AC1). Repointing `corpus.py:5` empties that grep and fails the assertion, so this change rewrites that module for the moved tree — the assertion AND its three old-path literals at `:5`, `:96`, `:102`; AC2 does not exclude `tests/unit/evals`. Also new in `d279`: `test_plan_replay_cli_paths.py:4` and `config_readers.py` above.\n- `evals/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py` keeps importing `rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay.legacy_v4_baseline` (research-to-src); `legacy_v4_baseline.py` stays the v4 formula's importable home because `evals/` is not on `sys.path`.\n\n## Scope\nThe moved trees; `rebar.toml`; `.gitignore`; `.github/codeql/codeql-config.yml`; the 3 scripts, the source/packaged-data files, the live docs, and the 20 test files enumerated above. Parent epic `e47b` AC2 carries the identical carve-outs, so leaf and parent agree. Deliberately NOT repointed: the moved tree's own 157 internal references (frozen as authored, above), `docs/adr/` (6 refs), `docs/archive/`, `docs/research/`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/release-notes.md`, `tests/fixtures/`, and generated `.test_durations`. AC2's grep excludes exactly that set.\n\n## Testing\n`python scripts/check_docs_index.py`; `python scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py`; `python evals/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py --root=.`; `python -m rebar.llm.plan_review.registry regenerate-criteria-guide` (the guide is GENERATED and must not be hand-edited); then `make verify`. Edge: `python -m build --wheel && unzip -l dist/*.whl | grep -c 'evals/'` prints `0`, sdist likewise; `git log --follow evals/plan-review-gate/replay/ledger.jsonl` shows pre-move history.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `docs/experiments` and `docs/calibration` are absent, and `evals/` contains exactly the union of the former `docs/experiments/**` and `docs/calibration/**` files — same total file count as the two trees had before the move, with `docs/calibration/**` now under `evals/calibration/**`.\n- [ ] `git grep -n 'docs/experiments\\|docs/calibration' -- . ':!docs/adr' ':!docs/archive' ':!docs/research' ':!CHANGELOG.md' ':!docs/release-notes.md' ':!tests/fixtures' ':!.test_durations' ':!evals' ':!tests/interfaces/contracts/test_removed_cli_verbs_heldout.py' ':!tests/interfaces/contracts/test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py' ':!tests/scripts/test_classify_gerrit_verify_change.py'` prints nothing — the three named files are the category-(c) freezes above.\n- [ ] The wheel contains no `evals/` entry, and the sdist contains no `evals/` entry.\n- [ ] `.github/codeql/codeql-config.yml` lists `evals/**` under `paths-ignore`.\n- [ ] `git diff -U0 -- docs/README.md` has exactly two hunks (lines 129 and 141).\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_docs_index.py` exits 0, proving no `docs/*.md` relative link still points into the vacated trees.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/evals/test_evals_corpus_root.py::test_no_hard_coded_roots` passes against the moved tree, and that module carries no `docs/experiments` literal.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"evals/","reason":"moved tree (from docs/experiments and docs/calibration)"},{"path":"docs/experiments/","reason":"removed"},{"path":"docs/calibration/","reason":"removed"},{"path":"rebar.toml","reason":"corpus_root = evals"},{"path":".gitignore","reason":"replay cache paths"},{"path":".github/codeql/codeql-config.yml","reason":"add evals/** to paths-ignore; docs/** no longer covers the moved tree"},{"path":"scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py","reason":"prefix"},{"path":"scripts/check_dco_identity.py","reason":"prefix"},{"path":"scripts/calibrate_completion_floor.py","reason":"cite"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_A1.md","reason":"rule text"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json","reason":"_comment paths"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/","reason":"spec comments + README"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/config_readers.py","reason":"[llm.evals] section comment names docs/experiments (new in d279)"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/corpus.py","reason":"docstring"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/legacy_v4_baseline.py","reason":"docstring"},{"path":"src/rebar/grounding/resolve.py","reason":"docstring"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/structured.py","reason":"docstring"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_advisory.py","reason":"docstring"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_operator_attested.py","reason":"docstring"},{"path":"docs/README.md","reason":"lines 129,141 only"},{"path":"tests/unit/evals/test_evals_corpus_root.py","reason":"d279's test_no_hard_coded_roots asserts corpus.py is the sole match; repointing corpus.py empties that grep"},{"path":"tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_cli_paths.py","reason":"module docstring cite (new in d279)"},{"path":"tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_corpus.py","reason":"path cite"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_interpreter_v2.py","reason":"path cite"},{"path":".rebar/evals/plan-review-project-failure-disposition-contract.eval.yaml","reason":"path cite"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_criterion_effectiveness.py","reason":"path"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_e6_agreement.py","reason":"path"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gate_eval_classifier.py","reason":"path"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_derive_code_review_threshold.py","reason":"path"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_impact_model_versioning.py","reason":"path"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ac_process_gate_criterion.py","reason":"path"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_asserted_capability_criterion.py","reason":"path"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_decomp_shape_criterion.py","reason":"path"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_necessity_criterion.py","reason":"path"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_project_failure_disposition_contract.py","reason":"path"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_t15_overlay_derisk_criterion.py","reason":"path"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_transition_force_flag_24f7.py","reason":"string"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py","reason":"string"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_check_criteria_vocabulary.py","reason":"string"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_check_dco_identity.py","reason":"string"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_classify_gerrit_verify_change.py","reason":"string"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["depends_on","d279-4cf9-d1a6-4f7b"],["parent","e47b-d3ef-338f-4bcd"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"e47b-d3ef-338f-4bcd","parent_status_uuid":"f288cf09-2a49-4ee1-89b4-ebdd50c796b6","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["complexity-red